==German==

===Etymology===
{{univerbation|de|ob|wohl}}, from the older use of {{m|de|ob}} as a conditional and concessive conjunction, reinforced with an adverb. Compare {{m|de|obgleich}}, {{m|de|obschon}}, {{m|de|obzwar}} and also {{m|de|gleichwohl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ɔpˈvoːl/}}
* {{audio|de|De-obwohl.ogg}}

===Conjunction===
{{head|de|conjunctions}}

# [[although]], [[though]], [[while]]
#: {{ux|de|Frau Anna, unsere Empfangsdame, flirtet mit Patienten, '''obwohl''' sie Mutter von drei Kindern ist.|Ms. Anna, our receptionist, flirts with patients, '''although''' she is the mother of three children.}}

====Usage notes====
Of all the synonyms, this is the most generally used option to introduce a concessive clause, and the only one for most speakers in everyday practice, excluding literary or formal custom.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|de|obgleich}}, {{l|de|wenngleich}}, {{l|de|trotzdem}}; {{l|de|gleichwohl}}; {{l|de|obzwar}}, {{l|de|wiewohl}}; {{l|de|obschon}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|de|ob}}
* {{l|de|wohl}}

